@ Acceptor
& acceptor
: Book glossary
A Tandu client species whose members possess specialized psychic abilities.

@ Akki
& akki
: Book glossary · Ah-kee
A neo-dolphin midshipman from Calafia serving aboard Streaker.

@ Gillian Baskin
& Gillian
& Baskin
& gillian baskin
: Book glossary
A human physician and Terragens Council agent serving on Streaker. She has undergone genetic modification.

@ Beie Chohooan
& beie chohooan
: Book glossary · Bay Choe-hoo-wan
A Synthian operative engaged in espionage. Synthians are among Earth's Galactic allies.

@ Brookida
& brookida
: Book glossary · Broo-kee-dah
A neo-dolphin metallurgist aboard Streaker.

@ Brothers of the Night
& brothers of the night
: Book glossary
An established Galactic patron species.

@ Calafia
& calafia
: Book glossary
A colony world shared by humans and neo-dolphins. Several Streaker crew members come from there.

@ Client
& client
: Book glossary
A species brought to sapience by a patron through uplift. Clients may still owe lengthy indentured service.

@ Creideiki
& creideiki
: Book glossary · Cry-dye-kee
The neo-dolphin captain of the Earth exploration ship Streaker.

@ Emerson D’Anite
& Emerson D'Anite
& Emerson
& emerson d’anite
: Book glossary
A human engineer aboard Streaker.

@ Charles Dart
& Dart
& charles dart
: Book glossary
A neo-chimpanzee planetologist aboard Streaker.

@ Derelict fleet
& derelict fleet
: Book glossary
Enormous abandoned ships from antiquity found by Streaker. Their discovery attracts the attention of rival Galactic powers.

@ Episiarch
& episiarch
: Book glossary
A psychic adept from a client species indentured to the Tandu.

@ Fem
& fem
: Book glossary
Anglic word referring specifically to a female human.

@ Fin
& fen
& fin
: Book glossary
Everyday term for a neo-dolphin; fen is the plural.

@ Galactic
& Galactics
& galactic
: Book glossary
A member of the ancient spacefaring civilizations spanning the Five Galaxies, many organized into patron-client lineages.

@ Gubru
& gubru
: Book glossary · Goo-broo
A birdlike Galactic species hostile to Earth.

@ Haoke
& haoke
: Book glossary · Ha-oh-kay
A Tursiops-type neo-dolphin.

@ Herbie
& herbie
: Book glossary
The crew's nickname for the preserved remains of an ancient starfarer of unknown origin.

@ Heurkea
& heurkea
: Book glossary · Hee-urk-eeah
A Stenos-type neo-dolphin.

@ Hikahi
& hikahi
: Book glossary · Hee-kah-hee
A female neo-dolphin who serves as Streaker's third officer.

@ Ifni
& ifni
: Book glossary
An expression connected with infinity and luck, sometimes personified as Lady Luck.

@ Iki
& iki
: Book glossary
An island associated with ancient destruction and death.

@ Toshio Iwashika
& Toshio
& Iwashika
& toshio iwashika
: Book glossary
A human midshipman from Calafia serving aboard Streaker.

@ Kanten
& kanten
: Book glossary
One of the few Galactic species openly friendly to Earth.

@ Karrank%
& Karrank
& karrank%
: Book glossary
A client species profoundly altered during indenture and damaged by the process. Its name cannot be accurately pronounced by humans.

@ Keneenk
& keneenk
: Book glossary
A discipline combining human-style analytical thought with dolphins' older Whale Dream tradition.

@ Keepiru
& keepiru
: Book glossary · Kee-peer-ooh
Streaker's chief pilot, originally from Atlast.

@ Kiqui
& kiqui
: Book glossary · Kee-kwee
Amphibious pre-sentient animals native to Kithrup, making them relevant to the question of uplift.

@ Krat
& krat
: Book glossary
Commander of the Soro forces.

@ K’tha-jon
& K'tha-jon
& k’tha-jon
: Book glossary · K’thah-jon
A Stenos-type neo-dolphin of a special variant and a petty officer aboard Streaker.

@ Library
& the Library
& library
: Book glossary
The immense shared Galactic archive of accumulated knowledge, traditionally traced to the Progenitors. Galactic civilizations depend heavily on it.

@ Makanee
& makanee
: Book glossary · Ma-kah-nay
Streaker's surgeon, a female neo-dolphin.

@ Man
& man
: Book glossary
In Anglic, a person of any sex.

@ Mel
& mel
: Book glossary
In Anglic, a male human.

@ Ignacio Metz
& Metz
& ignacio metz
: Book glossary
An uplift expert serving aboard Streaker.

@ Moki
& moki
: Book glossary · Moe-kee
A Stenos-type neo-dolphin.

@ The Niss Machine
& Niss Machine
& Niss
& the niss machine
: Book glossary
A limited artificial intelligence lent to Thomas Orley by Tymbrimi agents.

@ Thomas Orley
& Tom Orley
& Orley
& thomas orley
: Book glossary
A Terragens Council agent who has undergone mild genetic engineering.

@ Pila
& pila
: Book glossary
A Galactic patron species within the Soro clan that is hostile to Earth.

@ Primal Delphin
& primal delphin
: Book glossary
A partly structured ancestral communication mode used by natural, non-uplifted Earth dolphins.

@ Progenitors
& progenitors
: Book glossary
Legendary first intelligent beings credited with founding Galactic civilization and its Library billions of years ago.

@ Sah’ot
& Sah'ot
& sah’ot
: Book glossary · Sah-ote
A Stenos-type neo-dolphin and civilian linguist serving aboard Streaker.

@ Shallow Cluster
& shallow cluster
: Book glossary
An isolated, sparsely visited globular cluster where Streaker discovered the ancient fleet.

@ Soro
& soro
: Book glossary
A powerful Galactic patron species hostile to Earth, with its own interests in Streaker's discovery.

@ Stenos
& stenos
: Book glossary
A category of neo-dolphins whose ancestry includes genes from natural rough-toothed dolphins. Distinguished from Tursiops-type neo-dolphins.

@ Stenos bredanensis
& stenos bredanensis
: Book glossary
Earth's naturally occurring rough-toothed dolphin, whose genes contribute to some neo-dolphins.

@ Dennie Sudman
& Dennie
& Sudman
& dennie sudman
: Book glossary
A human exobiologist, or scientist studying life beyond Earth.

@ Hannes Suessi
& Suessi
& hannes suessi
: Book glossary
A human engineer aboard Streaker.

@ Synthian
& Synthians
& synthian
: Book glossary
A member of one of the Galactic species friendly to Earth.

@ Takkata-Jim
& takkata-jim
: Book glossary · Tah-kah-tah-jim
A Stenos-type neo-dolphin who serves as Streaker's vice-captain.

@ Tandu
& tandu
: Book glossary
A militant Galactic species hostile to Earth, associated with clients including Acceptors and Episiarchs.

@ Thennanin
& thennanin
: Book glossary · Thenn-an-in
A militarized Galactic species involved in the struggle over Streaker.

@ Tsh’t
& Tsh't
& tsh’t
: Book glossary · Tish-oot
A female neo-dolphin serving as Streaker's fourth officer.

@ Tursiops
& tursiops
: Book glossary
A crew term for neo-dolphins without Stenos genetic additions.

@ Tursiops amicus
& tursiops amicus
: Book glossary
Scientific name for the modern uplifted dolphin: 'friendly bottlenose'.

@ Tursiops truncatus
& tursiops truncatus
: Book glossary
Earth's natural bottlenose dolphin, ancestral to modern uplifted dolphins.

@ Tymbrimi
& tymbrimi
: Book glossary · Tim-brye-me
A Galactic species friendly to Earth, associated with ingenuity and cleverness.

@ Uplift
& uplifting
& uplift
: Book glossary
The process through which an established sapient species develops another species' intelligence through selective breeding, genetic engineering and education.

@ Wattaceti
& wattaceti
: Book glossary
A neo-dolphin noncommissioned officer aboard Streaker.

@ Anglic
& anglic
: Companion addition
A human language spoken by Streaker's crew; its vocabulary includes terms such as fem and mel.

@ Trinary
& trinary
: Companion addition
An expressive, patterned language form used by neo-dolphins, with rhythms and poetry unlike everyday Anglic.

@ Whale Dream
& whale dream
: Companion addition
An older cetacean heritage of memory, myth and nonhuman thinking that disciplines such as keneenk attempt to integrate with logic.

@ Patron
& patron species
& patron race
& patron
: Companion addition
A sapient species responsible for uplifting a less-developed species. Galactic society formalizes the relationship between patrons and clients.

@ Indenture
& indentured
& indenture
: Companion addition
The period of obligatory service a client species owes its patron following uplift.

@ Streaker
& streaker
: Companion addition
An Earth exploration vessel crewed chiefly by neo-dolphins, with human specialists aboard. Its discovery attracts several competing Galactic powers.

@ Kithrup
& kithrup
: Companion addition
An ocean-rich planet where Streaker takes refuge; its native life and environment affect the crew.

@ Neo-dolphin
& neo-dolphins
& neo-fin
& neo-fins
& neo-dolphin
: Companion addition
A dolphin uplifted by humanity to sapient intelligence, sometimes called a fin (plural: fen).

@ Neo-chimpanzee
& neo-chimp
& neo-chimps
& neo-chimpanzee
: Companion addition
A chimpanzee uplifted by humanity to sapient intelligence. Charles Dart is one.

@ Terragens Council
& terragens council
: Companion addition
A governing body representing humans and their uplifted species in interstellar affairs.

@ Five Galaxies
& five galaxies
: Companion addition
The extensive established Galactic civilization, connected by patron-client relationships. Earth is a relative newcomer.

@ Atlast
& atlast
: Companion addition
The home world of Streaker's chief pilot, Keepiru.

@ Pre-sentient
& presapient
& pre-sentient
: Companion addition
A species that has not developed full sapient intelligence but may be a candidate for uplift, such as Kithrup's Kiqui.

@ Humanity
& humans
& humanity
: Companion addition
Earth's sapient species, patron of uplifted dolphins and chimps, unusual in Galactic society for having no known patron.

@ Client race
& client race
: Companion addition
A species uplifted by a patron; it may be indentured or may have completed its obligations.

@ Galactic clan
& Galactic clans
& galactic clan
: Companion addition
A network of patron and client species whose shared uplift history creates political alliances and obligations.
